---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
	title="Classes and class packs"
	description="Sell multi-week pottery courses, drop-in sessions and class packs with waitlists that fill cancelled seats automatically."
>
	<section class="band-dark page-hero">
		<div class="wrap split">
			<div>
				<p class="eyebrow">Classes &amp; packs</p>
				<h1>Classes that fill themselves.</h1>
				<p class="lede">
					Six-week wheel courses, Saturday drop-ins, date-night hand-building, kids' camps. Set them up
					once and let students book, pay and reschedule without emailing you.
				</p>
				<a href="/contact" class="btn">Book a demo</a>
			</div>
			<img
				src="/images/class-pack.svg"
				alt="A six-class pack card with three classes used and a waitlist card for a Tuesday evening session"
				width="480"
				height="320"
			/>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap section narrow">
		<h2>Courses, drop-ins and packs</h2>
		<p>
			A course is a fixed series, like Wheel 101 on Tuesdays for six weeks. A drop-in is a single
			session anyone can book. A class pack is credit: sell a pack of 5 or 10 and students spend
			one credit per drop-in, with an expiry date you choose.
		</p>

		<h2>Waitlists that work while you sleep</h2>
		<p>
			When a class is full, students join the waitlist. If someone cancels, the next person on the
			list gets the seat offered by text and has two hours to accept before it moves on. Students
			receive a reminder the day before every class, with what to bring and where to park.
		</p>

		<h2>Instructors see their roster</h2>
		<p>
			Instructors get their own login with today's roster, who has paid, and who is new to clay. They
			can mark attendance from the studio tablet and leave notes for the next instructor.
		</p>

		<h2>Gift cards</h2>
		<p>
			Sell gift cards for any amount or for a specific course. December is the busiest month for most
			studios we work with, and gift cards are a big part of why.
		</p>
	</section>
</Base>
